  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Adaptation for Rural livelihoods Crisis Modifier-El Nino Induced drought</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be implemented through local Partners already implementing CARL2 projects namely, Aquaculture (Gutu), HOCIC (Bulilima) and LID Agency (Mberengwa) and SAFIRE (Buhera). Oxfam and partners will work with and through existing structures, local leaders, government stakeholders and beneficiary communities. Strong focus will be put in coordinating with local authorities and district civil protection/disaster management units, WASH, Food security, gender and protection sub committees to ensure sharing of information on initiative by different actors, identifying key relevant stakeholders and embed plans and capacity building into the local district planning and functioning In -kind food distributions targeting  individuals in Gutu, Mberengwa and Bulilima will be done for 5 months beginning November 2024 &#x2013; March 2025</narrative>
  </description>
